  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Self-reliance and poverty alleviation of refugees, IDPs and host communities through livelihoods, protection, and education programs in Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program combines two livelihood and protection interventions to enable people affected by displacement in Ethiopia to build self-reliance. Contract party Ethiopian Orthodox Church - Development and Inter-Church Aid Commission (EOTC-DICAC) will utilize the &#x201c;Graduation out of Poverty&#x201d; approach to provide sustainable pathways out of poverty for out-of-camp refugees and host communities in Addis Ababa. The desired result is sustainable self-reliance.

Implementing partner Jerusalem Children and Community Development Organization (JeCCDO) will undertake livelihood, protection, education, and capacity building programming in Debre-Birhan in Amhara  with women, children, and youth among the key target demographics. In addition to IDPs, the project will also benefit underprivileged host communities. By promoting inclusive development and strengthening local community structures, the project seeks to improve the overall well-being and resilience of the host community members, fostering social cohesion and integration for host communities and Internally Displaced Person (IDPs).</narrative>
  </description>
